Follows the hazard recorded in 9036b29c7 (diagnosed, not fixed). NO TEST WAS CHANGED: the repair is
an operator design call and the operator is asleep. Four options are costed with a recommendation in
docs/research-notes/test-suite-rewrites-the-record-survey-2026-07-29.md §6.

THE SURVEY THE HAZARD COMMIT SAID IT HAD NOT DONE

Method: three throwaway `git worktree --detach` checkouts on tmpfs; environment_files/ copied in
(without it the ARC tests abort early and the survey under-reports); PYTHONPATH pointed at the
worktree's python/ to defeat the editable install, which otherwise resolves `import carnot` to the
CANONICAL checkout and would have let a worktree run write into the real repo; `git status
--porcelain -uno` as the oracle. Per-test attribution inside a single run comes from a CPython audit
hook (sys.addaudithook) recording every in-repo write against the executing nodeid — which fires
INSIDE a runpy.run_path, where the writes actually happen.

The hazard commit's hypothesis was mostly wrong, and that matters. 20 test files runpy a path naming
an experiment script (only 2 name a path literally under scripts/experiments/ — the "11" was a looser
grep). Run one at a time in a clean worktree, EXACTLY ONE moves a tracked file:
test_experiment_3946_r11l_first_solve.py rewriting results/experiment_3946_r11l_first_solve.json,
which loses inference_substrate_correction_note, inference_substrate_original_invalid_value,
solve_provenance and solve_provenance_note. All 125 tests/python/test_arc_*.py, run individually,
move ZERO tracked files (the six that abort early in a worktree were re-run in the canonical repo
under the new detector: 67 passed, nothing moved). So the runpy class explains 1 of the 39 — a repair
aimed only at those call sites would look like a fix while leaving the rest in place.

THE GUARD THAT EXISTED AND DID NOT FIRE

determination_preservation_lint.py already refused dropping flagged_adversarial or a corrigendum*
record. It sat directly in the path of the exp3946 deletion and printed OK, because
inference_substrate_correction_note is a corrigendum in substance but its NAME lacks the string
"corrigendum". A guard that is trusted and silently fails to fire is worse than no guard.

WIDENED 2 rules -> 4. Rule 3: no top-level MARKER field may be dropped (correction / provenance /
disclosure / acknowledgment / retraction / caveat / review note / verifier_is_oracle /
preconditions_checked). Rule 4: a substrate or mode declaration may not be WEAKENED IN PLACE
(live_gpu -> cpu_training, real_model -> synthetic_runner, anything -> blocked) without a note that
NAMES that field. Values are principle-unwrapped first ({"principle":…, "value":…} — 162 artifacts,
the exact shape that was origin bug #2 of the QA-Layer Authenticity Discipline), and an unrecognised
substrate string ranks UNKNOWN, never WEAK.

The marker list is DERIVED, not wished for: a census of all 31,510 distinct top-level keys across the
15,331 results/**/*.json files, keeping name-shapes that mark a REVIEW OUTPUT and rejecting those
that mark a MEASUREMENT. `correct` is deliberately not a pattern — 601 artifacts carry
energy_correct / n_correct / judge_correct and fail-forward re-runs must be free to change them.

Calibrated over 1,200 commits (3,232 modified artifact pairs): rule 3 fires 10x, rule 4 fires 8x, and
EVERY rule-4 hit is a genuine instance of the hazard class — including one previously unknown,
results/experiment_911_drift_probe_tier0i.json taking real_model -> synthetic_runner FIVE times in
main, plus experiment_307 taking live_gpu -> cpu_training TWICE. Zero violations from either new rule
across the 8 commits since the lint first shipped.

NEW: scripts/test_suite_mutation_check.py

The broad, shallow half — "did this run modify tracked files, and which?", no opinion about content,
so it also covers openspec/ and output/ which the lint does not. --snapshot / --check / --restore,
--run -- <cmd> to wrap a run, and --gate wired as a pre-commit hook that refuses while
ops/.test_suite_mutation_pending.json exists. That marker is the interlock: an unattended agent that
runs the suite, sees the record move, then `git add -A && git commit`s is stopped rather than
publishing. Dogfooded end to end on the one confirmed offender against the canonical repo: caught,
restored, sha256 byte-identical before and after.

NEW: scripts/pytest_write_audit_plugin.py — the instrument, shipped so the survey is reproducible
after any repair rather than being a one-off anecdote.

TESTS: 50 passing across the three. The three confirmed incidents are replayed as fixtures, including
an explicit test that the timestamp class is DELIBERATELY not the lint's job — that boundary is what
keeps the lint from refusing ordinary fail-forward re-runs, which is how a guard gets switched off.
Also pinned: measurement fields containing "correct" are not protected; unknown substrate strings are
never read as downgrades; principle-wrapped substrates are unwrapped before ranking; one deletion
produces exactly one refusal line; and an unrelated *_change_note does not excuse a substrate
downgrade (a loose escape hatch found and removed during review — the same failure mode, reintroduced
inside its own fix).

THE RECORD IS INTACT: all 31,564 tracked files hashed at session start and again after; the only
differences are this session's deliberate edits. No results/**, openspec/** or output/** artifact
changed. The protected evidence directories were read only.

Spec: REQ-ARC-WMTE-6041 (+ REQ-ARC-WMTE-5995's implementation status cross-linked to the widening).

